{"schema_version":"1.7.5","id":"SUSE-SU-2025:4522-1","published":"2025-12-26T10:35:01Z","modified":"2026-03-23T04:50:23.569270Z","related":["CVE-2025-12084","CVE-2025-13836","CVE-2025-13837"],"upstream":["CVE-2025-12084","CVE-2025-13836","CVE-2025-13837"],"summary":"Security update for python39","details":"This update for python39 fixes the following issues:\n\n- CVE-2025-12084: quadratic complexity when building nested elements using `xml.dom.minidom` methods that depend on\n  `_clear_id_cache()` can lead to availability issues when building excessively nested documents (bsc#1254997).\n- CVE-2025-13836: use of `Content-Length` by default when reading an HTTP response with no read amount specified can\n  lead to OOM issues and DoS when a client deals with a malicious server (bsc#1254400).\n- CVE-2025-13837: data read by the plistlib module according to the size specified by the file itself can lead to OOM\n  issues and DoS (bsc#1254401).\n","affected":[{"package":{"name":"python39","ecosystem":"openSUSE:Leap 15.6","purl":"pkg:rpm/opensuse/python39&distro=openSUSE%20Leap%2015.6"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"3.9.25-150300.4.90.1"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"binaries":[{"libpython3_9-1_0":"3.9.25-150300.4.90.1","libpython3_9-1_0-32bit":"3.9.25-150300.4.90.1","python39":"3.9.25-150300.4.90.1","python39-32bit":"3.9.25-150300.4.90.1","python39-base":"3.9.25-150300.4.90.1","python39-base-32bit":"3.9.25-150300.4.90.1","python39-curses":"3.9.25-150300.4.90.1","python39-dbm":"3.9.25-150300.4.90.1","python39-devel":"3.9.25-150300.4.90.1","python39-doc":"3.9.25-150300.4.90.1","python39-doc-devhelp":"3.9.25-150300.4.90.1","python39-idle":"3.9.25-150300.4.90.1","python39-testsuite":"3.9.25-150300.4.90.1","python39-tk":"3.9.25-150300.4.90.1","python39-tools":"3.9.25-150300.4.90.1"}]},"database_specific":{"source":"https://ftp.suse.com/pub/projects/security/osv/SUSE-SU-2025:4522-1.json"}},{"package":{"name":"python39-core","ecosystem":"openSU